# Frontend Work: Design Skill + Zero Hardcoding

Applies to ALL frontend work (pages, components, shells, styling, layout, redesigns).
Read and follow this BEFORE starting any frontend task.

## 1. Always use the design-frontend skill

Before writing or changing any UI, read and follow the design skill at
`.agents/skills/design-taste-frontend/SKILL.md` (anti-slop rules, theme/color/shape
locks, icon-library usage, `next/font`, accessibility, em-dash ban, pre-flight check).
Do not freelance UI without it.

## 2. Never hardcode (colors, theme, tenant values)

Mirror how the landing page, login, and signup were built: nothing hardcoded.

- **Colors / theme**: components reference design tokens only. Define token VALUES once
  in `globals.css` (`:root`, `.dark`, and scoped blocks like `.admin-theme`), then use
  `var(--token)` everywhere. No raw hex, `rgb()`, or palette utilities (`slate-*`,
  `indigo-*`, `bg-black`, `text-white`) inside components.
- **Tenant-specific values**: never hardcode brand names, logos, copy, domains, etc.
  Pull them from tenant config / branding props (e.g. `branding.publicName`). The
  `atlas/no-hardcoded-tenant-strings` lint rule enforces this.
- **Light + dark**: every surface must support both modes via the `.dark` toggle, like
  the rest of the app. Never ship a mode-locked screen.

## 3. Dropdown & overlay transitions

Custom dropdowns, menus, popovers, and similar overlay panels must animate open/close.
Do not use unstyled native `<select>` on studio/admin form surfaces when a custom picker
is appropriate.

- **Shared primitives**: use `DropdownField`, `dropdownPanelClassName`, and
  `inlineExpandClassName` from `admin-form-dropdown-shared.tsx`.
- **Portaled panels**: `DropdownField` renders menus via `createPortal` on `document.body`.
  The panel root MUST include `admin-theme admin-dropdown-panel` so `--admin-*` tokens
  resolve (portals sit outside the shell). Default `portalZIndex` is `100`; use `85` inside
  modals (`z-[70]` overlays).
- **Enter motion**: panels use `motion-safe:animate-[admin-dropdown-in_0.18s_cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1)]`
  with `motion-safe:origin-top` (defined in `globals.css`).
- **Trigger affordance**: chevrons rotate with `transition-transform duration-200`.
- **Inline expand**: forms that reveal below a trigger (e.g. add-lesson) reuse
  `inlineExpandClassName` for the same motion language.
- **Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`**: always gate with `motion-safe:`; never ship
  animation-only feedback without a static fallback.

```tsx
// BAD: native select with no transition on studio form
<select className={selectClassName}>...</select>

// GOOD: custom picker with shared dropdown panel animation
<DropdownField ...>
  <div className={dropdownPanelClassName} role="listbox">...</div>
</DropdownField>
```

```tsx
// BAD: hardcoded color + tenant string
<div className="bg-[#6366F1] text-white">FundedBeyond Admin</div>

// GOOD: tokens + tenant config
<div className="bg-[var(--admin-primary)] text-[var(--admin-on-primary)]">
  {`${branding.publicName} Admin`}
</div>
```

## Pre-finish checklist (frontend)

- [ ] design-frontend skill consulted and applied
- [ ] no raw hex / palette colors / `bg-black` / `text-white` in components (tokens only)
- [ ] no hardcoded tenant strings (use branding/config)
- [ ] works in BOTH light and dark mode
- [ ] dropdowns/menus/popovers use shared transition primitives (`dropdownPanelClassName`, `inlineExpandClassName`)
- [ ] `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm lint` pass for changed files
